description:
crate-jmap-base-client/src/ws/mod.rs:162-170 clones `val` before `from_value(val)`, but the clone is only needed in the error path:

```rust
"StateChange" => {
    let raw = val.clone();                                // always allocated
    match serde_json::from_value::<StateChange>(val) {
        Ok(sc) => Ok(WsFrame::StateChange(sc)),           // raw discarded
        Err(_) => Ok(WsFrame::Unknown { type_name, raw }),
    }
}
```

Replacing with `StateChange::deserialize(&val)` (borrowing) lets the success path drop val and the error path move it into Unknown.

Why P3: only fires on hot WS frame paths. Negligible unless WS event spam is a real workload.

jmap-base-client is the foundation client crate per workspace AGENTS.md; coordinate any change with the canonical extension-client (jmap-mail-client) and its 6 siblings if a parallel pattern exists there.
